  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-905bb8bc Web logs overview\"**\n- URL: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-905bb8bc-web-logs-overview-fcce4e3bda3b\n- Six panels: total requests, unique client IPs, requests over time, responses by status code, top countries by requests, and top URLs.\n- Time range is set to 2026-10-01 through 2026-12-31. The sample timestamps run from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03, so a \"last 7 days\" default would show almost nothing.\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-905bb8bc 5xx spike\"**\n- ID: `38308e38-b070-4fcd-ae63-0faa7ab61cb0`, enabled, runs every 1m.\n- Type `.es-query` on `kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`, 5-minute window.\n- Counts documents where `response.keyword` matches `5*` and fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- No action connector is attached, so the rule will record alerts but won't notify anyone yet.\n- Status shows \"pending\" because it hasn't run its first check yet.\n\n**What the data looks like**\n- 14,074 requests from 1,001 unique client IPs and 448 distinct URLs.\n- Status codes: 200 (12,832), 404 (801), 503 (441). There are no other 5xx codes.\n- Top countries: CN, IN, US, ID, BR.\n\n**Things to know**\n- The current date is 2026-10-12, but the sample data is dated later, mostly after that. So the rule's 5-minute window may often be empty right now, and it may not fire until the data's timestamps reach the present.\n- The 5xx threshold of more than 10 in 5 minutes is a rate the sample data is unlikely to hit often. The 441 total 503s are spread across two months.\n- I used a wildcard on `response.keyword` rather than a range query, because the data view has `response` as a string.",
